Latest update (2026-10-08 14:01 UTC): expanded pinned Java `socksConstruction` from 93 to 109 actual constructor inputs and matched the added outcomes/reflected proxy values natively. The added cases establish that CR/U+2028/U+2029 do not terminate Java's `//` comments, a final root-level comment returns an empty route map while nested EOF truncation fails, and numeric `D`/`F`/`L` suffixes coerce to Java Double/Float/Long strings. Long suffix cases include signed bounds and a value above `Long.MAX_VALUE`. The native differential first exposed comment recovery and suffix handling mismatches; the parser now matches all 109 cases. The final fixture SHA-256 is `8a7a34c2268f78d46e9b7b909015db4217156d6040ee6b3908b31caa7e5c485a`.

